-71164" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338907 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338907 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\int \\frac{3}{2}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338907 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "83815382-7a50-585c-99ac-149a3085c008" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338907 #edb/ref 1074 "We can just take the constant factor out of the integral, and then apply the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{2}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int {x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}(\\frac{{x}^{5+1}}{5+1})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{6}}{6}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{6}}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534256 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186535094 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534256 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186535100 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534256 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186535141 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534256 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534256 #edb/ref 1045 "The Constant Multiple Rule for Indefinite Integrals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534256 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186535100 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534256 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534256 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048442 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534256 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "56e16704-8547-5154-b162-51ecdcf21e1b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534284 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{{y}^{8}}{6}+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534284 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534284 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0aa7dce6-df1a-5088-806d-df25a6f8ac37" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534376 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{10{z}^{5}}+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534376 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534376 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3a676b7a-83f4-580e-bc68-198c1d310014" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592